	// numbers.** EMPTY for every program that declares none, which is every program built by anything but
	// that command. See `TestDiscovery.DiscoveredTest` for why the mangled name and the prose both live
	// here rather than one being derived from the other.
	//
	// ⚠ **AN ARRAY AND NOT A MAP, because the ORDER is the fact being stored.** The index a test reports
	// under is its position in this list, and a report's reading order is this order; a keyed structure
	// would answer membership, which nothing asks.
	export var declaredTests as DiscoveredTestArray

	// ⭐⭐ **EVERY FREE FUNCTION'S NAMESPACE-QUALIFIED SPELLING ⇒ THE DIRECTORY THAT DECLARES IT** —
	// `utils.helper` for a `helper` declared in `utils/`, `lib.inner.deepHelper` for one in `lib/inner/`. THE
	// door a dotted CALLEE asks through to be read as a directory-qualified free call rather than as
	// `Type.method`.
	//
	// ⭐ **THE VALUE IS THE DIRECTORY BECAUSE A CONTESTED NAME REGISTERS EACH DECLARATION UNDER ITS
	// `<directory>~name` MINT**, and the written qualifier selects it (`namespaceQualifiedFunctionName`); for
	// an uncontested name the spelling only routes to the bare name.
	//
	// ⚠ **IT CARRIES NO VISIBILITY, ON PURPOSE.** A qualified call is resolved to a declared name and then
	// meets `SemanticCheck.calleeVisibleFrom` exactly as a bare call does — so `utils.hidden()` is refused by
	// the tier the declaration wrote, in that check's own words (E3008), rather than silently
	// becoming "no such function" here. Gating this map on the tier would move ONE decision into TWO places
	// and make the blunter message win.
	//
	// ⚠ **METHODS ARE ABSENT AND MUST STAY ABSENT.** A method is already keyed `Type.method`,
	// whole-program and namespace-free — so a `utils.Point.create` entry would be a second spelling of
	// a name that already has one, competing with the type reading of the same tokens for nothing.
	var namespaceQualifiedFunctions as NamespaceQualifiedFunctionMap

	// ⭐⭐ **THE MODULE DIRECTORY OF THE FILE THAT FIRST DECLARED EACH BARE FREE-FUNCTION NAME** — the
